    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen keys are mapped to `[C`/`]C`, jumping with those keys while follow mode is enabled causes cursors to be merged/deleted.\n\nMight be related:\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41836\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nyes 'test' | head -n5 | nvim --clean -c 'noremap <Up> [C' -c 'noremap <Down> ]C'\n```\n\n```\nvalQ\n<Down><Down><Down><Down><Down>\n```\n\n```\nvalQ\n<Up>\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe same behavior as when running `[C` or `]C` without a keymap: follow mode is enabled, but the cursors aren't merged/deleted when jumping.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1677+g e884c01bef\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Btw\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.17.0 (94e7c887)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
