        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> motion should never dedupe just by the primary overlap.\n> \n> Whereas if non-primary cursors overlap each other, they will never \"un-overlap\" on their own, so always dedupe in that case.\n\nThat model is implemented by https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42060\n\nThere is a small followup after that to close the  original issue described here.\n\n",
