        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It does mask the issue: when follow-mode is enabled, overlapping cursors are merged when moving:\n> \n> ```\n> V2jQ  -- set cursors, enables follow mode\n> [C    -- 3 left after jump\n> k[C   -- 2 left after jump\n> ```\n\nWith follow-mode=on,  `k` in this case moves the cursors up *beyond the buffer edge*. That is expected to lose a cursor, unless you are proposing cursors can go offscreen (https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41808), which seems a bit much.\n\nWhereas `[C` is a jump (absolute motion), and cursors won't follow it. https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42052",
            "created_at": "2026-09-24T11:47:45Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41995#issuecomment-5813471976",
